# 26. NFT evaluates the metrics

The next node is `_evaluate_node()`.

It finds a previous passing baseline:

```python
baseline = find_baseline(...)
```

It also reads error signals from logs:

```python
signals = read_log_signals(...)
```

Then calls:

```python
evaluation = evaluate(
    state["metrics"],
    settings,
    baseline,
    signals,
)
```

This calls:

`ag_nft/evaluate.py`

The rules are deterministic.

## Example performance rules

Default configuration:

```text
p95 target = 500 ms
p99 target = 1000 ms
error-rate target = 1%
```

Our results:

```text
p95 = 720 ms
p99 = 950 ms
error rate = 5%
```

The checks become:

```text
p95 latency       -> fail
p99 latency       -> pass
error rate        -> fail
```

The LLM is not involved in deciding these results.

## Category result

The `_outcome()` function applies:

```python
if any check is fail:
    category result = fail
elif any check is warn:
    category result = partial
else:
    category result = pass
```

So our outcomes might be:

```json
[
  {
    "category": "performance",
    "result": "fail",
    "throughput": 8.4
  },
  {
    "category": "load",
    "result": "fail",
    "throughput": 8.4
  }
]
```

The evaluation object contains:

```python
Evaluation(
    metrics=metrics,
    checks=checks,
    outcomes=outcomes,
    baseline=baseline,
    limitations=limitations,
    log_signals=signals,
)
```

