# 27. NFT asks the LLM for explanations

The next node is `_analyze_node()`:

```python
analysis = analyze(
    state["evaluation"],
    state["settings"],
    run,
    state.get("llm"),
)
```

This calls:

`ag_nft/analyzer.py`

The important rule is:

> The LLM explains the results. It does not determine the results.

If all checks pass, the system may avoid an LLM call:

```python
if all(c.status == "pass" for c in evaluation.checks):
    return template_analysis(evaluation)
```

If a check fails, the system can use tool mode or digest mode.

The model may produce:

```json
{
  "summary": "Refund performance exceeded the p95 target and showed an elevated error rate.",
  "check_explanations": {
    "perf.p95": "The 720 ms p95 is above the 500 ms target.",
    "load.error_rate": "Five percent of requests failed, exceeding the 1 percent limit."
  },
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "statement": "The refund service may be waiting on a downstream payment provider.",
      "confidence": "HYPOTHESIS",
      "related_check": "perf.p95"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Review downstream payment-provider latency.",
    "Check refund-service connection-pool limits."
  ],
  "limitations": [
